--TEST--
`Core\Response\Stream::end` ends the body, a second `end` does nothing, and a write after it throws and sends nothing — `rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-writes-as-a-stream`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Response\Stream::end
// A stream started with `$mustEnd` and then ended is not reported, so the run
// prints only what the program wrote and exits with 0.
var $body = Core\Response::stream("text/csv", null, null, "orders.csv");
$body->write("id,name\n");
$body->end();
$body->end();
try {
    $body->write("too late\n");
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}

// A stream started without `$mustEnd` can be ended too.
var $plain = Core\Response::stream("text/plain; charset=utf-8");
$plain->end();
echo "done\n";
--EXPECT--
id,name
Core\Response\Stream::write(): the stream has ended, because `end()` was called. Nothing was sent.
done
